摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness plugin for Fly.io Sprites: computers for agents. Sprites MCP tools and packaged workflow guidance for remote builds, tests, and long-running services.","id":"gh:1334459388","install_available":true,"language":"Python","name":"sprites-deepseek-plugin","slug":"superfly/sprites-deepseek-plugin","topics":["agent-plugin","agent-sandbox","ai-agents","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","fly-io","mcp","remote-development","sprites"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugin for Fly.io Sprites: computers for agents. Sprites MCP tools and packaged wor"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"kflow guidance for remote builds, tests, and long-running services."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Sprites for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Use Sprites from DeepSeek Harness: isolated, persistent Linux environments for builds, tests, experi"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ments, and long-running services."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"This repository is a Harness bundle. Its `cordis.patch.yml` mounts:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client`, connected to the hosted Sprites MCP server.\n- This package's `index"},{"id":"p5s2","text":".js` entry, which mounts `@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-filesystem` against the packaged Sprites workflow s"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"entry, which mounts `@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-filesystem` against the packaged Sprites workflow skill."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The result is a native Cordis composition: Sprites tools appear as `mcp__sprites__*`, and the Sprite"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"s skill is discoverable through Harness's normal skill system."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- Node.js 20.19 or newer. The packaged filesystem provider currently depends on Chokidar 5, whose en"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"gine floor is Node 20.19.\n- DeepSeek Harness developer preview.\n- Browser access for the first Sprit"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"es OAuth authorization.\n- Network access for `npx` to run the pinned `mcp-remote@0.1.38` OAuth bridg"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" OAuth authorization.\n- Network access for `npx` to run the pinned `mcp-remote@0.1.38` OAuth bridge."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Harness's current Streamable HTTP MCP transport accepts static headers but does not perform MCP OAut"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"h. This bundle therefore uses Harness's supported stdio transport and `mcp-remote` to complete the s"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"tandard browser OAuth flow without requiring a Sprites API token."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Install the GitHub checkout into the profile you use. For the built-in Web profile:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Then start that profile:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"On first connection, complete the browser OAuth flow, choose the Fly.io organization, and review the"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" connector access policy. Restart Harness once if the initial tool synchronization timed out while y"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ou were authorizing."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"For local development from this repository:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"To try the layer without installing it into a profile:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Verify the installed bundle and composed rows without booting the UI:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The output should include the `dsh-sprites-plugin` layer, `sprites-mcp`, and `sprites-skill-filesyst"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"output should include the `dsh-sprites-plugin` layer, `sprites-mcp`, and `sprites-skill-filesystem`."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## First prompts"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- \"List my sprites.\"\n- \"Create a sprite for this experiment and run `uname -a` in it.\"\n- \"Create a c"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"heckpoint, then run the test suite in my sprite.\"\n- \"Start the web service in my sprite and give me "},{"id":"p24s3","text":", then run the test suite in my sprite.\"\n- \"Start the web service in my sprite and give me its URL.\""},{"id":"p25s1","text":"An empty sprite list is a successful authenticated response."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Authentication and access"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The hosted endpoint is `https://sprites.dev/mcp` and uses OAuth 2.1. `mcp-remote` stores its OAuth s"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"tate in its normal local credential directory; this repository contains no credentials."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The Sprites consent screen normally creates a restricted connector token. Its default name prefix is"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" often `mcp-`, and it may cap how many sprites the connector can create. A custom non-empty prefix r"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"emains restricted. Choosing **Full access** removes the prefix restriction but grants access to ever"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"y sprite in the organization."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Prefer restricted access for agent work. If a create call reports a required prefix, Harness should "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"retry once with that exact prefix and report the actual name."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"`cordis.patch.yml` contributes two rows:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"1. `sprites-mcp` starts `mcp-remote` through the Harness MCP client. The bridge handles OAuth and ex"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"poses server tools through `ctx.tools` as `mcp__sprites__<tool>`.\n2. `sprites-skill-filesystem` load"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"s this package's `index.js`. The entry resolves `skills/` from `import.meta.url`, then mounts `@deep"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"seek-ai/dsh-skill-filesystem` as an isolated provider. This is intentionally done in JavaScript: a b"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"undle patch is evaluated with the profile directory as its `baseUrl`, not the installed package dire"},{"id":"p32s6","text":"patch is evaluated with the profile directory as its `baseUrl`, not the installed package directory."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"The MCP subprocess also sends fixed, privacy-safe client attribution headers:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| Header | Value |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| `Fly-Client-Agent` | `deepseek-harness` |\n| `Fly-Client-Interactive` | `false` |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"No user-, machine-, repository-, or session-specific attribution is sent. The headers are advisory a"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"nalytics only and are not used for authorization or rate limiting."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"`mcp-remote` includes both the server URL and serialized headers in its OAuth cache key. Changing ei"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"ther attribution header therefore invalidates existing cached authorization and requires users to au"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"header therefore invalidates existing cached authorization and requires users to authenticate again."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"## Safety"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"- Treat services exposed through a sprite URL as potentially internet-accessible.\n- Never publish se"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"crets, environment dumps, arbitrary files, debug endpoints, or unfiltered logs.\n- Use a checkpoint b"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"efore risky filesystem changes, dependency upgrades, or migrations.\n- Destroying a sprite is irrever"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"sible. Only destroy one when the user explicitly asks to delete, destroy, or remove it, or approves "},{"id":"p39s5","text":"cleanup.\n- Inspect outbound network policy before changing it."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Troubleshooting"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"### Tools are missing"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Confirm the bundle appears in `--dump-config` and that both Cordis rows are present. Harness's MCP c"},{"id":"p42s2","text":"lient logs connection, discovery, and tool-registration failures. The native tool names begin with `"},{"id":"p42s3","text":"ction, discovery, and tool-registration failures. The native tool names begin with `mcp__sprites__`."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"### OAuth did not finish"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"Keep the Harness process running while completing the browser flow. If initial synchronization times"},{"id":"p44s2","text":" out, finish authorization and restart Harness; `mcp-remote` reuses the stored OAuth session."},{"id":"p45s1","text":"For persistent `mcp-remote` authentication state problems, follow its upstream troubleshooting guida"},{"id":"p45s2","text":"nce. Clearing its credential directory signs every `mcp-remote` connector out, so do not do that cas"},{"id":"p45s3","text":"learing its credential directory signs every `mcp-remote` connector out, so do not do that casually."},{"id":"p46s1","text":"### `npx` cannot start"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"Make sure Node.js 20.19+ and `npx` are available in the environment that launches Harness. The MCP c"},{"id":"p47s2","text":"lient intentionally uses argument arrays without shell interpolation."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
